-- Tests for the cover: Articles 7 to 11 and the three layers together (`the outcome of`). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the percentages, day limits, periods and thresholds the
-- source prints, before the assertion was run; the working is beside each. A failing assertion is a
-- finding, never a value to edit. Sums insured, costs, dates and the two table percentages (which the
-- source does not contain) are hypothetical.
--
-- The base claim: an ordinary illness, a 5-day stay in Western medicine on 1-5 May 2026, standard
-- contract (20 million dong for each scope), first contract from 1 Jan 2026, cost 3,000,000.

§ `Tests, the cover`

§§ `Article 7, scope`

#ASSERT `the scope of` `III.3 surgery` EQUALS `scope C`
#ASSERT `the scope of` `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident` EQUALS `scope B`
#ASSERT `Article 7.3, the contract includes at least two of the three scopes` `the standard contract`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7.3, the contract includes at least two of the three scopes` (`a 2026 contract insuring` (JUST 1) NOTHING NOTHING))
-- 7.2: an accident is not a scope C event.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`claiming` `III.1 hospitalisation in Western medicine` `an accident` `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the benefit does not answer to the cause of the event (Article 7.2)`)
-- 7.1: Vietnam only.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`outside Vietnam` `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event was outside Vietnam (Article 7.1)`)
-- A scope the contract does not include.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 contract insuring` NOTHING (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000)) `the death claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the contract does not include the scope this benefit belongs to (Articles 7.2, 7.3)`)

§§ `Article 8, the programme`

-- "đến 20trđ" (up to 20 million) is standard, "trên 20trđ" (over) is special.
#ASSERT `Article 8, the programme for` `scope C` `under` (`a 2026 contract insuring` (JUST 1) (JUST 1) (JUST 20000000)) EQUALS `the standard programme`
#ASSERT `Article 8, the programme for` `scope C` `under` (`a 2026 contract insuring` (JUST 1) (JUST 1) (JUST 20000001)) EQUALS `the special programme`

§§ `Article 8 III.1 and III.2, hospital days`

GIVEN `admitted` IS A DATE
      `discharged` IS A DATE
      `cost` IS A NUMBER
      `used` IS A NUMBER
      c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`with a stay` `admitted` `discharged` `cost` `used` c MEANS
    `with the stay` (JUST (`a stay` `admitted` `discharged` NOTHING `cost` `used`)) c

-- Standard, 20 million: 0.5% is 100,000 a day for the first 10 days, 0.3% is 60,000 from the 11th.
-- 5 days: 500,000. 12 days: 10 x 100,000 + 2 x 60,000 = 1,120,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` `the illness stay claim` EQUALS `payable` 500000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 12) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 1120000
-- Special, scope C 50 million: 250,000 a day, then 150,000; 12 days cap 2,500,000 + 300,000 =
-- 2,800,000. A cost of 2,000,000 is paid in full; a cost of 9,000,000 is paid up to the cap.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` `the special contract` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 12) 2000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 2000000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` `the special contract` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 12) 9000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 2800000
-- 60 days a policy year: 55 already paid, a 10-day stay pays 5 days, 500,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 10) 3000000 55 `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 500000
-- III.4: a 6-month contract has 60 x 6/12 = 30 days; 25 used, a 10-day stay pays 5 days, 500,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a contract` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) 6 (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) 1 FALSE FALSE NOTHING) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 10) 3000000 25 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 500000
-- Eastern medicine: 0.2% is 40,000 a day; 10 days 400,000. 90 days a year: 85 used pays 5 days,
-- 200,000. A 7-month contract has 90 x 7/12 = 52.5 days; 50 used pays 2.5 days, 100,000 (no
-- rounding, fork F39).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`claiming` `III.2 hospitalisation in Eastern medicine` `an illness` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 10) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 400000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`claiming` `III.2 hospitalisation in Eastern medicine` `an illness` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 10) 3000000 85 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 200000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a contract` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 7 31) 7 (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) 1 FALSE FALSE NOTHING) (`claiming` `III.2 hospitalisation in Eastern medicine` `an illness` (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 10) 3000000 50 `the illness stay claim`))) EQUALS `payable` 100000
-- III.4 second paragraph: 19,800,000 already paid under scope C this year leaves 200,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the state` (`a state with payments of` 0 `under B and` 19800000 `under C`) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 200000
-- Article 3: another contract paid 2,000,000 of a 3,000,000 cost; special 5-day cap 1,250,000; Tasco
-- pays the 1,000,000 left.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with another contract paying` 2000000 (`with the contract` `the special contract` `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 1000000
-- A cost ordered by the insured's spouse is not a medical expense (2.16, 2.24; fork F38).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the doctor` (JUST (`The treating doctor` WITH `holds a lawful practising licence recognised by Vietnamese law` IS TRUE, `treating within the licence and the field of training` IS TRUE, `relation to the insured` IS `a spouse, parent, parent-in-law or child of the insured`, `registered to practise as required` IS TRUE)) (`with the contract` `the special contract` `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 0
-- 2.18: a 20-hour stay is no hospitalisation.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the stay` (JUST (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 20) 3000000 0)) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the stay is not a hospitalisation as Article 2.18 defines it`)
-- 4.4: a stay from 30 Dec 2026 to 3 Jan 2027, hours not recorded, counts 2 days in the contract:
-- 200,000. Counted in hours, it is declined.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 12 30) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 12 30) (YMD 2027 1 3) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 200000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 12 30) (`with the stay` (JUST (`a stay` (YMD 2026 12 30) (YMD 2027 1 3) (JUST 96) 3000000 0)) `the illness stay claim`))
-- 4.1: an event after the end date.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2027 1 2) (`with a stay` (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2027 1 6) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the contract was not in force on the day of the event (Article 4.1)`, `the consequence arose after the contract ended (Article 4.4)`)
-- Article 1: an insured with cancer at the start is not admitted.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the insured` (`The insured person` WITH `nationality and residence` IS `Vietnamese`, `date of birth` IS YMD 1990 3 15, `suffering from a neurological disease` IS FALSE, `suffering from a psychiatric disease` IS FALSE, `suffering from leprosy` IS FALSE, `suffering from cancer` IS TRUE, `permanent disability or injury, in percent` IS 0, `in a period of treatment for illness or injury` IS FALSE) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the insured is not a person Article 1 admits (Articles 1, 4.1(e))`)

§§ `Article 8 III.3, surgery`

GIVEN `percent` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `cost`    IS A NUMBER
      k         IS A `The contract`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a surgery claim at` `percent` `costing` `cost` `under` k MEANS
    `with the contract` k
        (`claiming` `III.3 surgery` `an illness`
            (`with the surgery` (JUST (`a surgery` (YMD 2026 5 2) `percent` `cost`)) `the illness stay claim`))

-- Standard: 10% of 20 million, 2,000,000. Special: 10% of 50 million is 5,000,000; a cost of
-- 4,000,000 is paid in full, one of 6,000,000 up to 5,000,000. No percentage: declined (X2).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a surgery claim at` (JUST 10) `costing` 4000000 `under` `the standard contract`) EQUALS `payable` 2000000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a surgery claim at` (JUST 10) `costing` 4000000 `under` `the special contract`) EQUALS `payable` 4000000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a surgery claim at` (JUST 10) `costing` 6000000 `under` `the special contract`) EQUALS `payable` 5000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of` (`a surgery claim at` NOTHING `costing` 4000000 `under` `the standard contract`)

§§ `Article 8 I and II, death and accident`

-- I.1: the whole sum insured.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` `the death claim` EQUALS `payable` 20000000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` `the special contract` `the death claim`) EQUALS `payable` 100000000

GIVEN b IS A `A benefit`
      j IS AN `An accidental injury`
      c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`an accident claim for` b `with` j `on` c MEANS
    `claiming` b `an accident` (`with the injury` (JUST j) c)

-- II.3 temporary injury, injury table 5% (hypothetical): standard 5% of 20 million, 1,000,000.
-- Special: 5% of 100 million is 5,000,000, cost 3,000,000 paid in full.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` `the accident claim` EQUALS `payable` 1000000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` `the special contract` `the accident claim`) EQUALS `payable` 3000000
-- II.2 partial permanent disability by loss, 30%: 6,000,000; no percentage: declined (X2).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`an accident claim for` `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `partial permanent disability by loss` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 30) 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`) EQUALS `payable` 6000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of` (`an accident claim for` `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `partial permanent disability by loss` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) NOTHING 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`)
-- II.4: 18,000,000 already paid under scope B leaves 2,000,000 of the 6,000,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the state` (`a state with payments of` 18000000 `under B and` 0 `under C`) (`an accident claim for` `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `partial permanent disability by loss` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 30) 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 2000000
-- II.1 with Article 9: death on 1 Aug 2026 (92 days after the accident); 3,000,000 paid before for
-- this accident: 20,000,000 - 3,000,000 = 17,000,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the state` (`a state with payments of` 3000000 `under B and` 0 `under C`) (`an accident claim for` `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `death` (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 8 1) NOTHING 0 3000000) `on` `the accident claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 17000000
-- Death 181 days after the accident (29 Oct 2026): outside Article 9.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`an accident claim for` `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `death` (YMD 2026 10 29) (YMD 2026 10 29) NOTHING 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the death or disability was not within 180 days of the accident (Article 9)`)
-- 4.4's exception: an accident on 1 Nov 2026, death on 15 Jan 2027, after the contract ended: paid.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) (`an accident claim for` `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `death` (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 1 15) NOTHING 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 20000000
-- Paralysis from an accident on 1 Nov 2026, certified 181 days later on 1 May 2027: it began within
-- the contract and within 180 days, and the certificate is not too early: paid (F17, F25).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) (`an accident claim for` `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `total permanent disability by paralysis or assessment` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 5 1) NOTHING 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 20000000
-- The same paralysis certified on day 179: too early (2.21(b)).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`an accident claim for` `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident` `with` (`an injury` `total permanent disability by paralysis or assessment` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 10 27) NOTHING 0 0) `on` `the accident claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the disability was certified earlier than Article 2.21(b) or 2.22(b) allows`)
-- Read literally (finding X17), a paralysis "occurs" when certified, and only day 180 satisfies
-- both Article 9 (within 180 days) and Article 2.21(b) (not before 180 days).
#ASSERT NOT (`Articles 9 and 2.21(b) read literally: a paralysis certified this many days after the accident qualifies` 179)
#ASSERT `Articles 9 and 2.21(b) read literally: a paralysis certified this many days after the accident qualifies` 180
#ASSERT NOT (`Articles 9 and 2.21(b) read literally: a paralysis certified this many days after the accident qualifies` 181)

§§ `Article 10, waiting periods`

-- Row 3, ordinary illness, 30 days from 1 Jan 2026: 30 Jan is day 29, 31 Jan day 30.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 1 30) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 1 30) (YMD 2026 2 3) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`)
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 1 31) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 1 31) (YMD 2026 2 4) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 500000
-- The illness began inside the period, the treatment after it: still inside (Article 10's definition).
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with treatment beginning on` (YMD 2026 2 15) (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 1 20) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 2 15) (YMD 2026 2 19) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`))) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`)
-- A reinstatement on 20 Apr 2026 restarts the count: 1 May is day 11.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the history` (`The history` WITH `the previous contract` IS NOTHING, `start of the insured's continuous participation` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `date of the most recent reinstatement` IS JUST (YMD 2026 4 20)) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`)
-- Accidents have none (row 1): an accident on 2 Jan 2026 is paid.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 1 2) (`with the injury` (JUST (`an injury` `temporary injury` (YMD 2026 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 2) (JUST 5) 3000000 0)) `the accident claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 1000000

-- A 5-day maternity stay in Western medicine from the given day; the flag is the 10.2(d) "miscarriage,
-- or a complication needing curettage".
GIVEN k     IS A `A maternity event`
      cur   IS A BOOLEAN
      `day` IS A DATE
      c     IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a maternity stay` k cur `day` c MEANS
    `with the maternity event` (JUST k) cur
        (`claiming` `III.1 hospitalisation in Western medicine` `maternity`
            (`with the illness` NOTHING
                (`with the event and treatment on` `day`
                    (`with a stay` `day` (`day` PLUS 4) 3000000 0 c))))

-- Row 5, complications, 90 days: 31 Mar 2026 is day 89, 1 Apr day 90. Row 6, childbirth, 270 days:
-- 28 Sep 2026 is day 270. Other maternity care has no row: declined.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a maternity stay` `a pregnancy complication` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 31) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`)
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a maternity stay` `a pregnancy complication` FALSE (YMD 2026 4 1) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 500000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a maternity stay` `childbirth` FALSE (YMD 2026 9 27) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`)
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`a maternity stay` `childbirth` FALSE (YMD 2026 9 28) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 500000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of` (`a maternity stay` `other maternity care` FALSE (YMD 2026 9 28) `the illness stay claim`)

-- Group contracts. 150 persons, a group: the over-100 column. Exactly 100: no column (finding X1).
GIVEN `persons` IS A NUMBER
      `group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `clause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `row 3` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The contract`
`a 2026 group contract of` `persons` `group` `clause` `row 3` MEANS
    `a contract` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 12 (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) `persons` `group` `clause` `row 3`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 100 TRUE FALSE NOTHING) `the illness stay claim`)
        BECAUSE "Article 10.1 has a column for contracts of under 100 persons and one for group contracts of over 100 persons, and none for a contract of exactly 100"
-- Rows 1 and 4 print the same figure in both columns, so an accident is answered even at 100 persons.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 100 TRUE FALSE NOTHING) `the accident claim`) EQUALS `payable` 1000000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 99 TRUE FALSE NOTHING) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 500000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 TRUE FALSE NOTHING) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `payable` 500000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `the illness stay claim`)
-- "or as agreed": a group contract that agrees 0 days for row 3 pays an illness on 2 Jan.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 TRUE FALSE (JUST 0)) (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 1 2) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 6) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`))) EQUALS `payable` 500000
-- Special disease in the first year: under 100 persons, excluded by 11.17; a group of 150 is not,
-- but waits 365 days (row 2); with the Article 10.2 clause it waits none.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the illness` (JUST `a special disease`) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST (`excluded by` `Article 11.17`))
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 TRUE FALSE NOTHING) (`with the illness` (JUST `a special disease`) `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `not payable` (LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`)
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 TRUE TRUE NOTHING) (`with the illness` (JUST `a special disease`) `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 500000
-- 10.2(d): childbirth on 16 May 2026, day 135, under the clause: half the benefit, 250,000; a
-- miscarriage on 15 Feb, day 45: 45/90 of it, 250,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 TRUE TRUE NOTHING) (`a maternity stay` `childbirth` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 16) `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 250000
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the contract` (`a 2026 group contract of` 150 TRUE TRUE NOTHING) (`a maternity stay` `a pregnancy complication` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 15) `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 250000
-- Second year: a special disease after a continuous renewal from 1 Jan 2025: row 2's 365 days and
-- 11.17's first year have both run.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the history` (`a renewal of` `the 2025 standard contract` `continuous since` (YMD 2025 1 1)) (`with the illness` (JUST `a special disease`) `the illness stay claim`)) EQUALS `payable` 500000
-- Finding: in a leap year, row 2's 365 days run out a day before 11.17's first year does.
-- Continuous participation from 1 Jan 2028: 31 Dec 2028 is day 365 and still the first year.
`the leap-year claim` MEANS
    `with the contract` (`a contract` (YMD 2028 1 1) (YMD 2028 12 31) 12 (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) 1 FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
        (`with the history` (`a first contract from` (YMD 2028 1 1))
            (`with the illness` (JUST `a special disease`)
                (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2028 12 31)
                    (`with a stay` (YMD 2028 12 31) (YMD 2028 12 31) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`))))
#ASSERT `Article 10, the waiting period has run` `the leap-year claim`
#ASSERT `Article 11.17 applies to` `the leap-year claim`
-- An increase serves its own waiting period (Article 5, second paragraph; F27): C raised from 10 to
-- 20 million at renewal; an illness on 15 Jan 2026 is past the 30 days counted from 1 Jan 2025 but
-- not those counted from 1 Jan 2026, so only 10 million is available: 5 x 0.5% x 10 million = 250,000.
#ASSERT `the outcome of` (`with the history` (`a renewal of` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 10000000)) `continuous since` (YMD 2025 1 1)) (`with the event and treatment on` (YMD 2026 1 15) (`with a stay` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 19) 3000000 0 `the illness stay claim`))) EQUALS `payable` 250000

§§ `Article 11, exclusions: each limb, and a near miss`

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of the event`
GIVETH A LIST OF `An exclusion of Article 11`
`the exclusions for a stay with` ks MEANS
    `Article 11, the exclusions that apply to` (`with the circumstances` ks `the illness stay claim`)

#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `an intentional act of a lawful heir of the insured`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.1`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `the insured took part in a fight, not confirmed as self-defence`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.14`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `alcohol, beer, drugs or a similar stimulant used by the insured caused it`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.2`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `the insured was driving a vehicle`) EQUALS EMPTY
-- 11.3, the limits as printed (F34): breath over 0.25, blood over 50; at the limit, not over.
GIVEN `breath` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `blood`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `driving` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `An exclusion of Article 11`
`the exclusions for readings` `breath` `blood` `driving` MEANS
    `Article 11, the exclusions that apply to`
        (`with alcohol readings` `breath` `blood`
            (`with the circumstances` (IF `driving` THEN (LIST `the insured was driving a vehicle`) ELSE EMPTY) `the illness stay claim`))

#ASSERT `the exclusions for readings` (JUST 0.26) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS LIST `Article 11.3`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for readings` (JUST 0.25) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the exclusions for readings` NOTHING (JUST 51) TRUE EQUALS LIST `Article 11.3`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for readings` NOTHING (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the exclusions for readings` (JUST 0.30) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `the insured was driving having used drugs, addictive or similar stimulant substances`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.3`
-- 11.4 needs no link to the event (finding X7): a traffic offence while driving excludes an illness stay.
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `the insured was driving a vehicle`, `the insured broke traffic law while driving a vehicle`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.4`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `the insured broke a rule of a local authority, an agency or a social organisation`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.4`
-- 11.5: treatment at a workplace medical unit, by an unregistered doctor, or against directions.
#ASSERT `Article 11, the exclusions that apply to` (`with the facility` (JUST (`a facility of kind` `a workplace medical unit`)) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.5`
#ASSERT `Article 11, the exclusions that apply to` (`with the doctor` (JUST (`The treating doctor` WITH `holds a lawful practising licence recognised by Vietnamese law` IS TRUE, `treating within the licence and the field of training` IS TRUE, `relation to the insured` IS `none`, `registered to practise as required` IS FALSE)) `the illness stay claim`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.5`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `treatment or medication not as the treating doctor directed`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.5`
-- 11.6, with 2.26 read literally (finding X6): climbing with gear is excluded, without gear is not.
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `aviation, other than as a ticketed passenger`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.6`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `taking part in` (`mountain or rock climbing` TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.6`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `taking part in` (`mountain or rock climbing` FALSE)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `taking part in` `boxing`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.6`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `training for or competing in a professional sport`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.6`
#ASSERT `the exclusions for a stay with` (LIST `hospitalisation for neurasthenia, physical debility, a mental disorder, a sleep disorder, insomnia, spinal degeneration or spina bifida`) EQUALS LIST `Article 11.7`
